<!-- TASKPLANNER:START -->
## TaskPlanner workflow

TaskPlanner 2.1.1 stores the git-tracked board in `.tasks/`.

- Read `.tasks/config.json` and the configured state files before project work.
- Select work from `NEXT.md`, then `BACKLOG.md`, honoring dependencies and priority.
- Keep one dependency-ready task in Next when no task is In Progress; leave Next empty while one task is In Progress.
- Move the complete task section before substantive work; never change a task ID.
- Because `aiPlanRequired` is true, retain or update the task's concise `### Plan`.
- A task is Done only when every acceptance criterion, verification, evidence output, evidence ceiling, and required commit/PR reference is present.
- Move completed tasks to `DONE.md`, add a top entry to `.tasks/WORK_LOG.md`, and update the Notion milestone only when its closure gate is met.
- Preserve all content outside TaskPlanner marker blocks.
<!-- TASKPLANNER:END -->
